match(1,'EtherChannel','Match each channel mode to its meaning.',[['LACP active','Initiate LACP negotiation'],['LACP passive','Respond to LACP negotiation'],['Static on','Bundle without negotiation'],['Port-channel','Logical bundled interface']],'Active and passive are LACP modes; static on lacks negotiation and requires carefully matched peers.','ether')
match(1,'VLANs & trunks','Match each VLAN term to its meaning.',[['Access VLAN','Data VLAN of an access port'],['Voice VLAN','Separate VLAN for phone traffic'],['Native VLAN','Normally carries untagged trunk traffic'],['Allowed VLAN list','Controls VLAN carriage on a trunk']],'A trunk carries only its allowed VLANs; native traffic is normally untagged, and an access port can also support a voice VLAN.','vlan')
match(1,'Wireless LANs','Match each wireless architecture term.',[['CAPWAP','AP-controller tunnel protocol'],['FlexConnect','Can switch client traffic at a branch'],['Monitor mode','Dedicated wireless monitoring'],['SSID','Wireless network name']],'Controller communication, forwarding location, AP operating mode and network identity are distinct wireless concepts.','wireless')
